## Priority 1: Critical Architecture, Data Integrity & Security

> [!CAUTION]
> These issues cause active runtime bugs, silent data drops, memory corruption, or security vulnerabilities under real workloads.

- [x] **P1.01 — Fix Context Window Overwrite & Immediate Eviction in DataLoader**
  - **Location:** [`optimizer.cpp:L87-119`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/learning/deepLearning/util/optimizer.cpp#L87-L119)
  - **Classification:** `Architecture` / `Data Loss Bug`
  - **Defect:** `Optimizer::ram_to_contextWindow` runs an internal `for` loop slicing through all windows in the 100k-token buffer. It overwrites `portion.context_window_tokens` and `portion.target_tokens` on each step without yielding or invoking training. On return, only the final window remains; all preceding windows (24,000+) are lost.
  - **Action Required:** Redesign into a sequential window iterator `bool get_next_context_window(Portion&, size_t& offset)` or accept a training callback:
    ```cpp
    template <typename Callback>
    void ram_to_contextWindow(Portion &portion, Callback &&train_step);
    ```

- [x] **P1.02 — Add Boundary & Null Pointer Validation to CUDA Bridge**
  - **Location:** [`transfer.cu:L22-63`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/learning/deepLearning/src/CUDA/transfer.cu#L22-L63)
  - **Classification:** `Security` / `Memory Safety`
  - **Defect:** `upload_to_gpu()` verifies `if (!gpu) return false;` but executes raw `cudaMemcpy` on `h_context` and `h_target` without validating that pointers are non-null and point to valid, allocated memory of size `context_elements * sizeof(__nv_bfloat16)`.
  - **Action Required:** Enforce rigorous input validation before DMA calls:
    ```cpp
    if (!gpu || !h_context || !h_target || context_elements == 0 || target_elements == 0) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Invalid memory parameters in upload_to_gpu\n");
        return false;
    }
    ```

- [ ] **P1.04 — Enforce File Size Caps & Ingestion Streaming Quotas**
  - **Location:** [`parser.cpp:L141-145`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/learning/deepLearning/util/parser.cpp#L141-L145)
  - **Classification:** `Security` / `Denial of Service (DoS)`
  - **Defect:** `tokenize_from_disk()` iterates with `while (parsed_data.get(byte))` appending to `input.tokenized_data` with no token quota or file size limit. Ingesting multi-gigabyte files exhausts physical host RAM.
  - **Action Required:** Check `std::filesystem::file_size()` against a strict maximum quota (e.g., 50 MB per file) and cap token emission per call.

- [ ] **P1.05 — Resolve Buffer Unit Mismatch (Tokens vs Brain Floats)**
  - **Location:** [`optimizer.hpp:L34-37`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/learning/deepLearning/include/optimizer.hpp#L34-L37) vs [`optimizer.cpp:L54-59`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/learning/deepLearning/util/optimizer.cpp#L54-L59)
  - **Classification:** `Logic Flaw` / `Resource Underallocation`
  - **Defect:** `ram_buffer_size = 100000` is documented as tokens ($100{,}000 \times 4 = 400{,}000$ floats). However, `disk_to_ram()` evaluates:
    ```cpp
    size_t brain_floats_needed = portion.ram_buffer_size - portion.ram_buffer_tokens.size();
    ```
    This allocates only 100,000 floats (25,000 tokens), starving the pipeline by 75%.
  - **Action Required:** Standardize units: define `ram_buffer_token_capacity = 100000` and compute `ram_buffer_float_capacity = ram_buffer_token_capacity * embedding_dim`.

- [ ] **P1.06 — Upgrade State Flags to Atomic Concurrency Primitives**
  - **Location:** [`optimizer.hpp:L26-27`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/learning/deepLearning/include/optimizer.hpp#L26-L27) and [`training.hpp:L15`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/learning/deepLearning/include/training.hpp#L15)
  - **Classification:** `Concurrency` / `Race Conditions`
  - **Defect:** `buffer_in_use`, `context_in_use`, and `training_in_use` are primitive non-volatile `bool` types without memory barriers. When decoupling disk streaming from GPU training across threads, this leads to torn reads, race conditions, and undefined behavior.
  - **Action Required:** Upgrade state locks to `std::atomic<bool>` or implement a synchronized channel with `std::mutex` and `std::condition_variable`.

