## Priority 2: Missing Core Neural Components & Algorithmic Stubs

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The architectural documentation specifies an end-to-end cognitive runtime; currently, the core AI math, GPU compute kernels, and training loops exist only as stubs.

- [ ] **P2.01 — Implement the AI Neural Nucleus & Forward Pass**
  - **Location:** [`ai.cpp:L3-15`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/learning/deepLearning/src/ai.cpp#L3-L15) and [`ai.hpp:L58-73`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/learning/deepLearning/include/ai.hpp#L58-L73)
  - **Classification:** `Core Feature` / `Machine Learning`
  - **Current State:** `AI::AI` sets weights, biases, and forward pass to `0.0`. `Key_Concepts` uses scalar `double` instead of tensor representations.
  - **Action Required:** Implement weight matrix storage ($W \in \mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{out}} \times d_{\text{in}}}$), bias vectors ($b$), dot-product matrix multiplication, activation functions (ReLU, GELU, SwiGLU), and loss calculation (MSE/Cross-Entropy).

- [ ] **P2.02 — Develop GPU Compute Kernels (Tensor Core GEMM on sm_89)**
  - **Location:** [`transfer.cu`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/learning/deepLearning/src/CUDA/transfer.cu)
  - **Classification:** `CUDA` / `GPU Acceleration`
  - **Current State:** The CUDA library only performs DMA memory transfers (`cudaMemcpy`). No device kernels exist for mathematical computation.
  - **Action Required:** Author CUDA kernels for:
    - Matrix multiplication (`forward_gemm_kernel` using WMMA/MMA instructions or cuBLASLt)
    - Vectorized activation evaluation (`relu_forward_kernel`)
    - Mean Squared Error / Cross-Entropy loss computation kernel.

- [ ] **P2.03 — Build Training Orchestration & Backpropagation Loop**
  - **Location:** [`training.cpp:L5-12`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/learning/deepLearning/src/training.cpp#L5-L12)
  - **Classification:** `Core Feature` / `Training Engine`
  - **Current State:** `Training::training()` instantiates a local empty `Portion` and invokes `ram_to_contextWindow()` once with zero feedback.
  - **Action Required:** Implement an end-to-end training loop:
    1. Read buffer from disk (`disk_to_ram`)
    2. Extract context window + target (`ram_to_contextWindow`)
    3. Upload to device VRAM (`upload_to_gpu`)
    4. Compute forward pass and loss
    5. Compute gradients and update weights (`optimizer_step` / AdamW)
    6. Advance sliding window.

- [ ] **P2.04 — Replace Container Byte Parsing with Modality Preprocessing**
  - **Location:** [`parser.cpp:L33-42`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/learning/deepLearning/util/parser.cpp#L33-L42)
  - **Classification:** `Algorithm` / `Multimodal Semantics`
  - **Defect:** Reading raw container bytes from `Photo.jpeg`, `Video.mp4`, and `Voice.ogg` causes the network to train on compressed container metadata (EXIF, Huffman trees, atom headers) rather than actual visual/acoustic features.
  - **Action Required:** Integrate proper media decoders:
    - Images: Raw RGB/grayscale pixel patch extraction
    - Audio: Mel-frequency spectrogram extraction
    - Video: Decoded frame sampling and patch projection.

- [ ] **P2.05 — Add Modality ID Bounds Checking & Collision Prevention**
  - **Location:** [`parser.hpp:L40-46`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/learning/deepLearning/include/parser.hpp#L40-L46)
  - **Classification:** `Algorithm` / `Namespace Safety`
  - **Defect:** If text vocabulary exceeds 9,999,999 entries, `next_text_id` increments directly into the number modality space (`10,000,000+`), corrupting categorical isolation.
  - **Action Required:** Enforce upper-bound assertions in `add_assign_increase`:
    ```cpp
    if (next_id >= MODALITY_UPPER_BOUND) {
        throw std::overflow_error("Exceeded modality ID partition capacity");
    }
    ```

- [ ] **P2.06 — Implement Chunked Streaming for Embedding Generation**
  - **Location:** [`parser.cpp:L75-103`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/learning/deepLearning/util/parser.cpp#L75-L103)
  - **Classification:** `Memory Optimization` / `Scalability`
  - **Defect:** `Parser::embedding()` accumulates all 33.15M `bfloat16_t` floats in `input.embedded_data` in host RAM before calling `save_data`.
  - **Action Required:** Stream dense vectors to disk in fixed batches (e.g., 64k tokens per flush) to keep RAM usage bounded regardless of dataset scale.

