## Priority 4: Production SaaS & Enterprise Architecture

- [ ] **P4.01 — Implement HTTP / gRPC Service Ingestion & Inference Layer**
  - **Classification:** `SaaS Infrastructure` / `API Layer`
  - **Defect:** Engine operates solely as a local console executable (`main.cpp`).
  - **Action Required:** Expose high-throughput REST / gRPC service endpoints:
    - `POST /v1/datasets/ingest` — Stream and tokenize multimodal inputs
    - `POST /v1/training/jobs` — Initiate background training runs
    - `GET  /v1/training/jobs/{id}` — Query training progress, step metrics, and loss
    - `POST /v1/inference/predict` — Execute forward prediction on context windows.

- [ ] **P4.02 — Asynchronous Task Queue & Job Management**
  - **Classification:** `SaaS Infrastructure` / `Task Scheduling`
  - **Action Required:** Integrate a job queue (Redis / RabbitMQ / internal threadpool) to handle long-running training and embedding jobs asynchronously with support for cancellation, retries, and job status tracking.

- [ ] **P4.03 — Multi-Tenancy & Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)**
  - **Classification:** `SaaS Security` / `Multi-Tenancy`
  - **Action Required:** Enforce tenant namespace isolation for datasets, checkpoints, and dictionary tables; implement API key authentication and token rate limiting per tenant.

- [ ] **P4.04 — Structured Logging, Metrics & Telemetry (OpenTelemetry / Prometheus)**
  - **Classification:** `Observability` / `SRE`
  - **Action Required:** Replace unstructured `std::cout` calls with structured JSON logging; emit real-time Prometheus metrics:
    - Training loss per step
    - Tokens processed per second
    - PCIe DMA transfer latency
    - GPU VRAM consumption & temperature
    - Health check endpoints (`/healthz`, `/readyz`).

- [ ] **P4.05 — Cloud Object Storage Integration (S3 / GCS / Azure Blob)**
  - **Classification:** `Storage Infrastructure` / `Cloud Native`
  - **Action Required:** Implement cloud storage connectors for streaming raw media assets and persisting checkpoint weights directly to AWS S3 or Google Cloud Storage.

- [ ] **P4.06 — Dynamic Configuration Management**
  - **Classification:** `Configuration` / `Config-as-Code`
  - **Action Required:** Externalize hardcoded hyperparameters (`ram_buffer_size`, `context_window_size`, `embedding_dim`, learning rate) to YAML/JSON configuration files and environment variables.

---

## Priority 5: DevOps, Packaging & Deployment Standards

- [ ] **P5.01 — Multi-Stage Containerization (Docker / OCI)**
  - **Classification:** `DevOps` / `Containerization`
  - **Action Required:** Create a multi-stage `Dockerfile`:
    - **Stage 1 (Builder):** NVIDIA CUDA 12.x/13.x devel image with C++23 compiler and build tools.
    - **Stage 2 (Runtime):** Lightweight CUDA runtime image containing only compiled binaries and shared libraries.

- [ ] **P5.02 — Decouple Application and Test Build Targets in Makefile**
  - **Location:** [`Makefile:L21-24`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Brain/Makefile#L21-L24)
  - **Classification:** `Build Optimization` / `Modularity`
  - **Defect:** `APP_SRCS` and `TEST_SRCS` both compile all files in `src/`, `test/`, and `util/` together.
  - **Action Required:** Separate application sources (`main.cpp` + `src/` + `util/`) from test harnesses (`test/*.cpp` + `util/`) so production binaries do not package unit test code.

- [ ] **P5.03 — Automated CI/CD Pipelines**
  - **Classification:** `DevOps` / `Continuous Integration`
  - **Action Required:** Configure GitHub Actions / GitLab CI workflow:
    - Automated compilation on pull requests
    - Execution of the 62-test verification harness
    - Static analysis (clang-tidy, cppcheck) and memory sanitation (ASan / LSan).
